    "Feature catalogs in edi and crysta contain stale planned statuses; inspect adapter/model/bindings and checked-in tests instead.",
    "CW is constant wavelength. Double b2b is the double back-to-back exponential TOF profile. FCJ is Finger-Cox-Jephcoat. March is March-Dollase.",
    "X-ray polarization optics correction does not imply support for polarised-neutron diffraction.",
    "edi exports single-crystal/total-scattering type tokens and an abstract ScExperimentBase, but its only concrete experiment family is BraggPdExperiment. Tokens or carried fields alone are not counted as implemented physics.",
    "diffraction-lib has six local/global minimiser adapters (LMFIT leastsq and least_squares, BUMPS LM/AMOEBA/DE, DFO-LS), plus BUMPS DREAM and emcee sampling. edi delegates fitting to crysta LM; named descent policies are not separate minimiser algorithms or MCMC.",
    "Tests cited here were inspected as evidence, not executed during this source audit.",
    "The functionality overview is the union across the two projects, not their intersection. The following comparison separates the implementations.",
    "The shared checklists preserve the 11 original chart areas. Filled widths equal implemented items divided by listed items. A feature qualifies in at least one compatible beam mode/backend; no claim of support in every combination is implied.",
    "Peak-profile coverage tracks eight reference families, not a count of all kernels. crysta additionally has pure CW Gaussian/Lorentzian/pseudo-Voigt profiles outside that reference list.",
    "The deterministic optimiser checklist counts LM once regardless of adapter or descent policy. Analytic derivatives are implemented by crysta, but are not counted as a separate optimiser.",
    "Single-crystal means a working single-crystal experiment/calculation path. Generic nuclear structure factors in the powder engine do not qualify as single-crystal workflow support.",
    "diffraction-lib cylinder absorption is CW-only; reciprocal TOF calibration is stored but not sent to its backends. crysta implements these missing TOF/absorption capabilities."
